Rename libvmaf's static feature-extractor `close()` callbacks so they can no
longer hijack libc `close()` in full-LTO builds on macOS/arm64.

On Darwin clang gives every *external* C symbol an ELF-style asm label, so
`close()` declared in <unistd.h> reaches the IR as `@"\01_close"`, while a
`static` function keeps the plain IR name `@close`. LLVM's LTO resolver keeps
those two apart, but after resolution both map onto the same flat Mach-O
symbol name `_close` in the single merged codegen unit. libvmaf's feature
extractors each define a `static int close(VmafFeatureExtractor *)`, so once
libvmaf is linked into ffmpeg/ffprobe the linker can bind libavformat's
`file_close()` call to one of those callbacks with completely different calling
conventions:

    close + 28:  ldr x20, [x0, #0x30]     ; x0 is a raw fd, not a fex
    close + 32:  ldr x0, [x20, #0x8]
    EXC_BAD_ACCESS at 0x33 (== fd 3 + 0x30)

which crashes ffprobe/ffmpeg with SIGSEGV every time an input file is closed.

Give every static `close` callback in libvmaf/src/feature its own unique name
(<file>_close) and update the corresponding VmafFeatureExtractor initializer.
(cambi.c already used close_cambi.)

This is the same class of defect as FFmpeg trac ticket #11479.

diff -ruN a/libvmaf/src/feature/ciede.c b/libvmaf/src/feature/ciede.c
--- a/libvmaf/src/feature/ciede.c	2023-12-07 13:27:32
+++ b/libvmaf/src/feature/ciede.c	2026-10-10 15:18:50
@@ -372,7 +372,7 @@
                                          index);
 }
 
-static int close(VmafFeatureExtractor *fex)
+static int ciede_close(VmafFeatureExtractor *fex)
 {
     CiedeState *s = fex->priv;
     if (s->ref.data[0] && s->dist.data[0]) {
@@ -391,7 +391,7 @@
     .name = "ciede",
     .init = init,
     .extract = extract,
-    .close = close,
+    .close = ciede_close,
     .priv_size = sizeof(CiedeState),
     .provided_features = provided_features,
 };
